## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

**Summary: 10 tests, 7 Critical findings, 1 Medium — this suite is almost entirely coverage-touching code that verifies nothing.**

---

### 🔴 CRITICAL — Tests giving false confidence

#### 1. Coverage-Touching Pattern (systemic — entire suite)
**Lines 6–89** | All 10 tests

This is a textbook coverage-touching suite. Every public method on `ProductCatalog` is called in declaration order, with names like `*_Works`, but **7 of 10 tests have no meaningful assertion**. This explains your 95% coverage with production bugs — the tests exercise code paths without verifying outcomes.

---

#### 2. No Assertions — 4 tests with zero assertions

| Test | Line | What's untested |
|---|---|---|
| `AddProduct_Works` | 17 | Never verifies the product was actually stored |
| `UpdatePrice_Works` | 32 | Never verifies the price actually changed |
| `RemoveProduct_Works` | 39 | Never verifies the product was actually removed |
| `GetProductCount_Works` | 63 | Calls `GetProductCount()`, discards the result |
| `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` | 69 | Never verifies any price was reduced |
| `ImportFromCsv_Works` | 85 | Never verifies any products were imported |

**Fix example — `AddProduct_Works`:**
